1. General Sizing Rules of Thumb
Standard Recommendation: Most Sybase experts recommend sizing tempdb at 10% to 25% of your total user database size. For a 1.5 TB database, this equates to 150 GB – 375 GB.
Conservative Starting Point: Some SAP/Sybase help guides suggest a more modest starting point of roughly 6-7% for initial setups. For 1.5 TB, this would be approximately 100 GB. 

-- Identify sessions consuming tempdb space
select spid, loggedindatetime, (@@maxpagesize * convert(int, pssinfo(spid, "tempdb_pages"))) / 1024 as USAGE_IN_KB
from master..sysprocesses where convert(int, pssinfo(spid, "tempdb_pages")) > 0 order by USAGE_IN_KB desc
go
